                        "entry_id": "a5ecaddb-7b3c-331e-bd28-16cc88e0b054",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any moth in the species-rich family Noctuidae or the superfamily Noctuoidea."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f0dc113-d4ab-444c-aacf-4fbc80805583",
                                "sense_id": "85ec3d38-3142-3b19-bfe9-ccbccd84c9ef",
                                "text": "Mr. H. McKnight, who resides at Goldstream, took a number of noctuids in September, feeding on hops."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f6d179c-0569-4e4f-81e3-26e118884440",
                                "sense_id": "85ec3d38-3142-3b19-bfe9-ccbccd84c9ef",
                                "text": "The total wing area of these moths were essentially the same (geometrids = 3.8 cm²; noctuids = 3.6. cm²). Consequently, wing-loading of the noctuids was about twice as high as in the geometrids."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef8641bb-cc6b-4b2c-a8b4-9bc895366f27",
                                "sense_id": "85ec3d38-3142-3b19-bfe9-ccbccd84c9ef",
                                "text": "Noctuids are renowned for their propensity for carnivory in general, and for cannibalism in particular (Gould et al. 1980)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
